WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:02.277
- [Narrator] Primetime game shows,

00:00:02.277 --> 00:00:06.295
(game show host speaks Chinese)

00:00:06.295 --> 00:00:08.520
(contestant speaks Chinese)

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:09.940
- [Narrator] military parades,

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:11.760
(soldiers chant)

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:13.590
and bookstores with dedicated sections

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:16.500
to the writings of
Chinese leader Xi Jinping.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.110
These are some of the ways
China's propaganda machine

00:00:19.110 --> 00:00:22.464
has elevated Xi's standing
to levels unseen in decades.

00:00:22.464 --> 00:00:25.464
(Xi speaks Chinese)

00:00:27.958 --> 00:00:28.791
(crowd applauds and cheers)

00:00:28.791 --> 00:00:30.210
- [Narrator] Over his 10 years as leader,

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.430
Xi has tried to orchestrate
the country's rise

00:00:32.430 --> 00:00:34.080
as a global superpower,

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:36.240
despite the recent slowdown in the economy

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:37.830
and pushback from the West.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:41.430
- He really has overturned

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:45.000
the way China has been governed.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.410
- [Narrator] So as Xi prepares to secure

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:48.270
a third term as president,

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:49.830
we break down these three moments

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:50.970
along his path to becoming

00:00:50.970 --> 00:00:53.043
one of China's longest-serving leaders.

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:56.760
Xi joined the Communist Party in 1971,

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.410
and steadily climbed through its ranks

00:00:58.410 --> 00:01:00.300
over the next few decades.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:02.640
In 2007, he rose to the national stage

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.950
when he joined the Politburo
Standing Committee,

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:07.560
a group of China's most senior officials.

00:01:07.560 --> 00:01:12.560
- The party elite actually
was craving a strong leader.

00:01:12.729 --> 00:01:14.700
(audience applauds)

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:18.720
When Xi Jinping came
to power in late 2012,

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:22.380
the party's power brokers
got what they wanted,

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:23.373
and then some.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:27.870
- [Narrator] The new
leader's change in approach

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:29.520
was put on display right away,

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:31.410
when Xi visited the city of Shenzhen

00:01:31.410 --> 00:01:33.900
to lay out his vision for the country.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.790
And he chose a symbolic venue,

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.487
an exhibition called "The
Road to Rejuvenation."

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:40.890
In a highly orchestrated moment

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:42.780
that was broadcast on state TV,

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:43.770
Xi was surrounded

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.680
by some of China's most
historical objects.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:48.330
- The display told the story

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:52.590
of China's rise from
subjugation to triumph

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:56.100
under the Chinese Communist
Party's leadership.

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:57.810
- [Narrator] And here,
Xi unveiled the name

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.180
for what would be the next
stage in China's story,

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:01.537
with him at its helm.

00:02:01.537 --> 00:02:03.217
(Xi speaks Chinese)

00:02:03.217 --> 00:02:08.217
- "China Dream" is a slogan
that conveys Xi Jinping's desire

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:11.520
to make China a global superpower

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:13.833
that is equal to the United States.

00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:16.530
- [Narrator] In the
early stages of his rule,

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:18.900
Xi tried to make China's economy more open

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:20.700
and driven by market forces.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:21.720
- He actually laid out

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:24.480
this very ambitious
economic reform program,

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.640
which called for state companies

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:29.370
to operate more like commercial firms,

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:33.450
and for the government to
promote entrepreneurship.

00:02:33.450 --> 00:02:35.700
- [Narrator] He also shattered
taboos in Chinese politics

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:37.110
by targeting party elders

00:02:37.110 --> 00:02:39.690
in a wide-ranging
anti-corruption campaign,

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:42.060
which ended up being
popular with the public.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:46.230
- He honed a very
paternalistic public image

00:02:46.230 --> 00:02:50.670
as Xi Dada, or Big Papa Xi.

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.070
- [Narrator] And Xi also
challenged the US more forcefully

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:54.423
than his predecessors.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.060
Xi's territorial ambitions

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:58.950
in regions including the South China Sea,

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:02.040
and economic programs such as
the Belt and Road Initiative,

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:04.710
began to clash with US interests.

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:06.870
- His China Dream also meant

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:11.280
putting China on a collision
course with the United States,

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:14.190
as China, you know, strove to be

00:03:14.190 --> 00:03:19.190
a rival economically,
militarily, and politically.

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:24.330
- [Narrator] And this collision
was about to come to a head

00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:27.363
when Xi invited President
Donald Trump to visit Beijing.

00:03:29.190 --> 00:03:32.010
- I remember on Trump's
first day in Beijing,

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:37.010
Xi Jinping and his wife
escorted Trump and his wife

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:40.893
on a private tour of the Forbidden City.

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:44.010
- [Narrator] Xi's plan
was to charm his rival

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:45.480
and calm the simmering tensions

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:47.040
created during his leadership.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:50.050
- There can be no more important subject

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:53.073
than China-US relation.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:58.500
- Xi Jinping tried to convince him

00:03:58.500 --> 00:04:01.290
that there's still so much to gain

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:06.290
from having a good
relationship with Beijing.

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:09.480
But it didn't really work.

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:10.770
- [Narrator] A few months after the visit,

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:13.620
the US imposed a series of
tariffs and trade barriers

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:14.610
on China.

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:16.140
Washington said it was in response

00:04:16.140 --> 00:04:19.500
to unfair trade practices and
intellectual property theft.

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:21.720
This began a trade war
that upended markets

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.910
and reshaped global commerce.

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:28.910
- The trade war lasted two
years, and both sides cut a deal.

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:32.820
It didn't really help
improve the relationship.

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:35.550
- [Narrator] The trade deal
was only a temporary truce.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:36.600
Soon after it was signed,

00:04:36.600 --> 00:04:38.580
the coronavirus pandemic began,

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.950
sinking the relationship even further.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:45.420
- This horrible thing that
was delivered by China,

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:46.253
and it was by China,-

00:04:46.253 --> 00:04:47.520
- [Narrator] The US President blamed China

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:48.900
for unleashing the virus,

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:51.153
a charge Beijing vehemently denied.

00:04:52.620 --> 00:04:54.180
The growing schism between the countries

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:56.760
only made Xi look more powerful at home,

00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:59.220
as the man who had stood up to the US.

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:01.110
And he ensured that he
would remain at the top

00:05:01.110 --> 00:05:03.570
by removing term limits in 2018,

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:06.840
paving the way for him to become
China's president-for-life.

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:11.550
- He tried to roll back
China's decades-long evolution

00:05:11.550 --> 00:05:14.850
toward Western-style,
you know, capitalism.

00:05:14.850 --> 00:05:19.710
This different path is
basically socialism,

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:22.713
you know, in the spirit of Mao Zedong.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.790
- [Narrator] And the spirit
of Mao was on full display

00:05:26.790 --> 00:05:30.270
in 2021, at the Communist
Party's centennial celebration

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:32.130
in Tiananmen Square.

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:35.250
- We saw the TV footage of Xi Jinping

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:37.200
wearing this Mao suit,

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.780
and standing behind this, you know, podium

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:42.767
adorned with hammer and sickle.

00:05:42.767 --> 00:05:45.210
("The Internationale")

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.860
- [Narrator] After a speech, Xi sang along

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:49.110
to "The Internationale," a socialist song

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:51.840
that, in China, has long
symbolized declarations of war

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:54.003
by the working class on capitalism.

00:05:56.280 --> 00:05:59.010
And it soon became clear
that this war was being waged

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:02.100
at some of China's most
valuable tech companies.

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:04.170
- Private technology firms

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:07.590
have grown tremendously in recent years,

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:10.350
but increasingly are seen

00:06:10.350 --> 00:06:15.350
as challenging Xi Jinping's
authoritarian rule.

00:06:15.708 --> 00:06:18.570
(Jack Ma speaks Chinese)

00:06:18.570 --> 00:06:20.640
- [Narrator] For Xi, they were
gaining too much influence

00:06:20.640 --> 00:06:24.540
in areas like finance,
entertainment, and digital gaming.

00:06:24.540 --> 00:06:28.470
- It was almost like a 180-degree turn.

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:32.040
He now is trying to further enhance

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:37.040
the role of the state, the
government, in running economy.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:39.060
- [Narrator] But even as Xi has continued

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:41.310
to concentrate his power
over the past decade,

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:43.290
he's also faced challenges,

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:45.600
from the pro-democracy
movement in Hong Kong

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:47.550
to Covid lockdowns that
have added pressure

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:48.870
to an economic slowdown

00:06:48.870 --> 00:06:50.943
weighed by a battered property market.

00:06:52.470 --> 00:06:53.700
And as Beijing and Washington

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:56.070
continue to compete for global influence,

00:06:56.070 --> 00:06:57.870
Xi is carrying on with his dream

00:06:57.870 --> 00:07:00.420
of making China a superpower.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:04.803
- As far as he is concerned,
China's time has arrived.

